		{"id":"d41a72457807790c","type":"text","text":"#### Apple Music","x":642,"y":-680,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"92b008c15874fed3","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nGood. Most important functions are at most one or two clicks away and there is minimal delay.\n**Satisfaction**\nEasy to use, beautiful design\n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nEverything is pretty clearly labeled and has iconography. Some Features like Automix might need some introduction first, but are easily memorized after.\n**Safety**\n“Dangerous” functions like removing albums require confirmation.\nthere’s also the system wide “shake to undo” on iOS, which works with apple Music\n\n","x":980,"y":-960,"width":310,"height":480,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1c298a92a8246e7b","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nThe Steam Controller is very effective and efficient to use once you learn how to use it. It’s incredible, especially for any mouse interfaces!\n**Satisfaction**\nIt is satisfying to use, but due to its age, the vibration motor and tactile feelings isn’t up to modern standards.\n**Learnability / Memorabilty**\nDifficult. It’s very different to a normal controller, since instead of a stick and dpad, it uses two touch pads. \n**Safety**\nThere is nothing to report here.\n\n\n","x":-455,"y":-820,"width":368,"height":411,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"211dfb4af79a3718","type":"text","text":"#### Steam Controller","x":-32,"y":-440,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#1068c6"},
